# Shared base: what the librarian agent itself needs at run time.
#
# Every bench runs the agent in-process, so every bench's lock includes this.
# It mirrors `[project].dependencies` in the root pyproject.toml, minus the two
# server packages (fastapi, uvicorn) that only orchestrator.py needs — a bench
# on the --via-api path talks to an orchestrator running in the repository's own
# .venv, not in the bench environment.
#
# The repository is not a package (`[tool.uv] package = false`), so the code
# arrives via PYTHONPATH rather than an install; only its dependencies are here.
# Keep this in step with pyproject.toml by hand — there is no check that would
# catch a drift, and a missing one surfaces as an ImportError on first run.
